<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Warna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1731</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Warna was concluded in 1731 between Shahu, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> king at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satara">Satara</a>, and his cousin Sambhaji II of Kolhapur, ending their long rivalry over the Maratha throne. Sambhaji accepted Shahu's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over most of the Maratha lands, while Kolhapur kept a separate territory south of the Warna river. It created the two lines of Satara and Kolhapur, and the Kolhapur kingdom lasted until 1949.</p></div>
